31,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The logs show nine conflicts died out because no one owned the problem. The minutes reveal the same flats held spots for five years without review.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,The sticker register shows households would pay to avoid equal claims! And four mornings had someone shifting bikes. It’s a real bottleneck!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Four mornings required shifting bikes. The rain exposure is also critical; spots past the downpipe stay wet, ruining saddles.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,The ledger is empty. No capital funds exist. Any new frame or repair means a direct levy on us. The treasurer spends three hours a month just counting coins.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The minutes confirm the covered spots were never reviewed. The rain data shows the exposed rows are genuinely unusable in winter.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, the minutes confirm the stagnation. If we don't review the allocation, the same households will keep the best spots forever.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, I agree! The sticker register proves people want a fair system, not just equal claims. We need to fix this!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, the shifting confirms the bottleneck. But the rain data is worse; exposed spots are unusable in winter.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, the rain makes the exposed spots useless, but the ledger is empty. We can't fix the roof without a levy.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, a levy is a recurring burden. I need to know if the physical effort of maintaining the rows justifies the cost.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, a levy is a recurring burden. I need to know if the physical effort of maintaining the rows justifies the cost.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Shunichi, I hear you, but the sticker register shows people are willing to pay for fairness! Maybe a small fee covers the roof?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the ledger is empty, but the rain data is undeniable. We need a solution that works without new capital.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Yumi, people pay for fairness, not for empty promises. I need to see the ward cycle park rates to know the real alternative cost.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, the ward park is an escape, not a fix. I need to know if the physical maintenance here is manageable before we accept any recurring cost.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, the ward park is a backup, not a solution. I need to know if the current arrangement is sustainable before we consider external costs.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Shunichi, I agree the park is just a backup. But if we can’t fix the roof, maybe we rotate the spots to share the rain fairly?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, rotating spots ignores the rain gradient. The eaves are fixed; moving bikes doesn't stop the water. We need a structural fix, not just a shuffle.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, structural fixes cost money we don't have. I need the supplier’s frame trial data to see if a cheap, temporary cover is viable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, a temporary cover is a recurring maintenance task. I need to know if the physical effort is sustainable before we accept the cost.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
