60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option C removes the ownership that caused the nine dead conflicts. If no one owns a spot, no one can be displaced.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,Option C sounds so freeing! No more arguing over who gets the dry spot. But will the double-tier racks be easy to use for everyone?,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C solves the morning bottleneck. No shifting, no ownership disputes. But I need to know if the racks handle the rain exposure.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option C ignores the empty ledger. Without capital, those racks are a fantasy. I need to know the actual cost before we dream.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option C requires constant physical management. I need to know if the effort to keep those racks clear is sustainable for one person.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, the racks are a one-time cost, not a recurring levy. The ledger is empty, but the conflict cost is higher.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Shunichi, I agree the cost is a worry! But the sticker register showed people would pay for fairness. Maybe we can fund the racks that way?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, the sticker register shows willingness, not capacity. The ledger is empty. I need the supplier’s trial data to verify if the racks are actually affordable.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, the supplier’s trial is the only number that matters. If the racks cost more than the ward park, we are just paying for the privilege of complaining.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, the racks are a one-time cost, but the daily clearing is a recurring physical burden. I need to know if that effort is sustainable.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, the effort is minimal. It is just moving a bike, not heavy lifting. The real cost is the social friction we avoid.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I agree! It’s just a quick move, not heavy lifting. Plus, the sticker register shows people want fairness, so they’ll help keep it tidy!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, the racks reduce the shifting I observed. The rain is still a factor, but the structure is more stable than the current rows.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, the racks are a one-time cost, but the daily clearing is a recurring physical burden. I need to know if that effort is sustainable.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, the effort is minimal, but the risk of it lapsing is high. I need a clear, low-burden protocol to ensure it doesn't die like the last two roles.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, a simple rotation of clearing duties prevents burnout. The social cost of inaction is higher than the physical effort.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I agree! A simple rotation works. Plus, the sticker register shows people want fairness, so they’ll help keep it tidy!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, I agree. A rotation prevents burnout. The racks solve the bottleneck and rain issues better than the current rows.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, I am not the one who will be clearing racks at dawn. I am the one who will be paying the levy. I need the supplier’s quote to know if this is a trap.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, the quote is a number, but the rotation is the safety net. If the cost is high, we need the protocol to be even simpler.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
